1
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:08,200
Montricoux is a fortified medieval village perched on high ground along the pilgrimage route to Santiago de Compostela,

2
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:11,700
a place of passage and a very important crossroads.

3
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:16,180
Indeed, from a heritage perspective, this is the postcard view of the village.

4
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:21,660
It gives the impression of a remarkably harmonious ensemble.

5
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:25,940
At first glance, one notices this octagonal bell tower,

6
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:33,100
built in red brick in the typical architectural style of Toulouse,

7
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:38,600
constructed in the 16th century, with a spire that truly stands out as a landmark.

8
00:00:39,380 --> 00:00:40,880
It is officially listed as a historic monument.

9
00:00:40,990 --> 00:00:43,940
Then behind it, one begins to perceive

10
00:00:44,330 --> 00:00:48,620
the 12th-century keep, built in cut limestone,

11
00:00:48,790 --> 00:00:51,460
marking the site of the former Templar settlement,

12
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:56,120
a crucial defensive stronghold during the Middle Ages in the 12th century.

13
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:00,080
There was once a castle around it, though not the same castle that exists today.

14
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:03,360
There was also an old church that formed part of the complex

15
00:01:03,580 --> 00:01:04,940
since this was a Templar site.

16
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:10,040
At that time, it was really a fortified stronghold rather than a true village or town.

17
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:14,540
The timber-framed houses came much later.

18
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:18,460
They appeared between the 15th and the 18th centuries.

19
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:25,540
We have this historical layer, and below it we can glimpse the old ramparts.

20
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:31,680
Below that lies the mill and the spillway over the Aveyron river.

21
00:01:32,750 --> 00:01:34,580
In my role as an Architect of Historic Buildings in France,

22
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:37,720
Montricoux is considered a remarkable heritage site.

23
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:45,519
We are currently developing regulations that truly help preserve and enhance this village

24
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:46,840
and tell its story.

25
00:01:47,130 --> 00:01:50,460
There are two types of protection in place.

26
00:01:50,690 --> 00:01:54,280
First, we have the historic heart of the old village center

27
00:01:54,410 --> 00:01:57,960
which is governed by a preservation and enhancement plan

28
00:01:58,780 --> 00:02:02,200
including detailed building records that explain each structure’s history,

29
00:02:02,530 --> 00:02:07,240
its specific features, and both its exterior and interior architecture.

30
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:10,560
Everything inside is protected just as much as the exterior.

31
00:02:11,140 --> 00:02:14,899
In doing so, we discover many magnificent elements

32
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:16,320
that tell the story of this place.

33
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:19,720
All of this is documented in individual records

34
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:22,300
which explain how restoration or intervention can be carried out,

35
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,320
what has no heritage value,

36
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:25,680
what does not contribute to heritage,

37
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:26,880
and what truly constitutes heritage,

38
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:28,840
as well as how it can be adapted

39
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:33,880
to contemporary ways of living

40
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:36,760
while still enriching ourselves through it.

41
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:37,620
It is a source of pride.
